BufferedReaderPartialBodyFilter::consume without a local buffer passed the inner reader's consume
through unchanged. That returns the inner reader's buffer from the old cursor on, which can extend
past the current partial body chunk into the next chunk's length header and data, while buffer()
and data*() cut it at the end of the chunk. A reader on top that returns consume's result, like
HashedReader::data_consume with fix-hashed-reader-data-consume.patch, then hands those bytes to
its caller as packet data, so they are parsed a second time. Cut the returned slice at the end of
the chunk as well.

With fix-hashed-reader-data-consume.patch applied and without this patch, a message of nested
partial-body compressed data packets (32 KB) yields a secret subkey with 67 KB of key material made
of the input read twice, and Key4::fingerprint then panics (see fix-key4-public-len.patch). With
this patch the subkey is parsed as at the pin, without the patch series.

The test in parse/partial_body.rs reads a partial body chunk of 4 octets followed by a final chunk;
without the patch consume returns the next chunk's header and data as well.

diff --git a/openpgp/src/parse/partial_body.rs b/openpgp/src/parse/partial_body.rs
index 43bf2b62..21472081 100644
--- a/openpgp/src/parse/partial_body.rs
+++ b/openpgp/src/parse/partial_body.rs
@@ -378,10 +378,13 @@ impl<T: BufferedReader<Cookie>> BufferedReader<Cookie>
             &buffer[self.cursor - amount..]
         } else {
             // Since we don't have a buffer, just pass through to the
-            // underlying reader.
-            assert!(amount <= self.partial_body_length as usize);
+            // underlying reader, but don't return data beyond the
+            // current chunk.
+            let chunk = self.partial_body_length as usize;
+            assert!(amount <= chunk);
             self.partial_body_length -= amount as u32;
-            self.reader.consume(amount)
+            let data = self.reader.consume(amount);
+            &data[..cmp::min(data.len(), chunk)]
         }
     }
 
@@ -424,3 +427,28 @@ impl<T: BufferedReader<Cookie>> BufferedReader<Cookie>
         &mut self.cookie
     }
 }
+
+#[cfg(test)]
+mod test {
+    use super::*;
+
+    #[test]
+    fn consume_stays_within_chunk() {
+        // A 4-octet partial body chunk followed by a final 3-octet
+        // chunk.
+        let data = b"abcd\x03XYZ";
+        let reader = buffered_reader::Memory::with_cookie(
+            &data[..], Cookie::default());
+        let mut pbf = BufferedReaderPartialBodyFilter::with_cookie(
+            reader, 4, true, Cookie::default());
+
+        assert_eq!(pbf.data(2).unwrap(), b"abcd");
+        // consume returns the buffer including the consumed data,
+        // which ends with the chunk, not with the inner reader's
+        // buffer.
+        assert_eq!(pbf.consume(2), b"abcd");
+        assert_eq!(pbf.buffer(), b"cd");
+        assert_eq!(pbf.consume(2), b"cd");
+        assert_eq!(pbf.data_eof().unwrap(), b"XYZ");
+    }
+}
